                        "entry_id": "7f8b5f7d-b5de-3442-8c52-ecda8e541bad",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "pardine"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f771e171-3c03-35b8-9555-d97faa227226",
                        "entry_id": "7f8b5f7d-b5de-3442-8c52-ecda8e541bad",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Interjection familière qui a souvent le sens de bien sûr, naturellement."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated",
                            "familiar"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b63951f6-f833-4a3d-84ca-5e0169b2687a",
                                "sense_id": "f771e171-3c03-35b8-9555-d97faa227226",
                                "text": "— Pourriez-vous me dire comment elle est devenue si rondelette.\n— Pardi, en se crevant de mangeaille comme vous et moi."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d4122974-0ea5-4123-b34e-c70abf6ee5b4",
                                "sense_id": "f771e171-3c03-35b8-9555-d97faa227226",
                                "text": "— Vrai ! elle avait quelqu’un ? disait une petite vendeuse, nouvelle au comptoir. — L’homme des bains, pardi ! répondait Clara."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "91732542-5eeb-4920-97dc-6677c5945db5",
                                "sense_id": "f771e171-3c03-35b8-9555-d97faa227226",
                                "text": "— Voilà un homme qui lui rendra un fameux service.\n— Lequel ? demanda Thérèse.\n— Celui de la dégoûter des hommes, pardi !"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "62909b60-7dd4-4dfb-b4fa-87a8c125ca08",
                                "sense_id": "f771e171-3c03-35b8-9555-d97faa227226",
                                "text": "« Tout de même, dit un jour Marion, tu comprends ça, toi.\n– Quoi ?\n– Eh bien ça, pardi, qu’on meure. »"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e32e83cc-d78c-4cad-b219-7bf74e2cc7ef",
                        "source_entry_id": "7f8b5f7d-b5de-3442-8c52-ecda8e541bad",
                        "source_sense_id": "f771e171-3c03-35b8-9555-d97faa227226",
                        "target_lang_word": "of course",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "of course",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cac0daff-dedd-3b6c-81c0-4c7c7b5a6a52",
                                        "entry_id": "c42ffe39-4d2b-315f-8cdd-3cbffe0f6570",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In due course; as a matter of course, as a natural result."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a78ee3e-3873-4fbf-bc4d-0ca90ed6fe0e",
                                                "sense_id": "cac0daff-dedd-3b6c-81c0-4c7c7b5a6a52",
                                                "text": "He inspired love and emulation wherever he appeared; envy and jealous rage followed of course; so that he became a very desirable, though a very dangerous acquaintance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d672d6eb-a44d-4beb-8dbd-c2330c6786b5",
                                                "sense_id": "cac0daff-dedd-3b6c-81c0-4c7c7b5a6a52",
                                                "text": "Not tarrying long enough in the brain to be subject to reflection, the next sensations, of course, obliterate them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27cb1587-3f16-4c45-97a6-740d1e8f6c6c",
                                                "sense_id": "cac0daff-dedd-3b6c-81c0-4c7c7b5a6a52",
                                                "text": "It was at one time made a question whether giving the royal assent to a single bill did not of course put an end to the session."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ce6e8dcc-872e-3c76-8d7f-8fedee7dddbe",
                                        "entry_id": "c42ffe39-4d2b-315f-8cdd-3cbffe0f6570",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Naturally, as would be expected; for obvious reasons, obviously."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9e956e3-4caa-4b49-8cdc-b872d6063f85",
                                                "sense_id": "ce6e8dcc-872e-3c76-8d7f-8fedee7dddbe",
                                                "text": "Of course I know that!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "607f6e1b-1e78-447a-8d09-af3f64fcf9fc",
                                                "sense_id": "ce6e8dcc-872e-3c76-8d7f-8fedee7dddbe",
                                                "text": "You will of course surrender all your future rights to the property."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a278154c-23ef-487a-9003-f4b8be2b8dd3",
                                                "sense_id": "ce6e8dcc-872e-3c76-8d7f-8fedee7dddbe",
                                                "text": "“Heavens!” exclaimed Nina, “the blue-stocking and the fogy!—and yours are pale blue, Eileen!—you’re about as self-conscious as Drina—slumping there with your hair tumbling à la Mérode! Oh, it's very picturesque, of course, but a straight spine and good grooming is better.[…]”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e194b264-8fec-4150-b7ea-910be20c54ec",
                                                "sense_id": "ce6e8dcc-872e-3c76-8d7f-8fedee7dddbe",
                                                "text": "We tiptoed into the house, up the stairs and along the hall into the room where the Professor had been spending so much of his time. 'Twas locked, of course, but the Deacon man got a big bunch of keys out of his pocket and commenced to putter with the lock."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b6e7f4b-668b-40f3-9acf-d6b5b33d5039",
                                                "sense_id": "ce6e8dcc-872e-3c76-8d7f-8fedee7dddbe",
                                                "text": "There were other flapper-era starlets, of course—Louise Brooks, Greta Garbo—but they were poseurs by comparison."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86c7f231-3981-4c8b-9542-3941db21f092",
                                                "sense_id": "ce6e8dcc-872e-3c76-8d7f-8fedee7dddbe",
                                                "text": "Risk is everywhere. From tabloid headlines insisting that coffee causes cancer (yesterday, of course, it cured it) to stern government warnings about alcohol and driving, the world is teeming with goblins. For each one there is a frighteningly precise measurement of just how likely it is to jump from the shadows and get you."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "of course",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "10de03ea-4830-3936-9ceb-e54cda5713da",
                                        "entry_id": "5ed0b4ec-5153-30e1-9605-f765525b994c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That is part of ordinary behaviour or custom; customary, natural."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08cdb8be-d9d0-4696-ab2e-77426ec86ffa",
                                                "sense_id": "10de03ea-4830-3936-9ceb-e54cda5713da",
                                                "text": "Had Francesca grown up by his side, she would have loved him; and a thousand indulgences, the result of careless good-nature, would have linked the child to the parent, till the mutual affection would have become a thing of course."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63dfc190-bb8d-43bd-83f3-c351eb67794d",
                                                "sense_id": "10de03ea-4830-3936-9ceb-e54cda5713da",
                                                "text": "I am not using a mere phrase of course, when I say that the feelings with which I bear a part in the ceremony of this day, are such as I find it difficult to utter in words."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "of course",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7c0cabfd-8175-3931-811c-36b7db26c929",
                                        "entry_id": "1228b4fa-82f3-3f78-8041-9ba82a848a48",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Indicates enthusiastic agreement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb4106eb-9f8d-4e74-b6dd-05e3cbc63672",
                                                "sense_id": "7c0cabfd-8175-3931-811c-36b7db26c929",
                                                "text": "Will you come with me? — Of course!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f57d90a9-fed9-3934-a9d9-66f55bf6221a",
                                        "entry_id": "1228b4fa-82f3-3f78-8041-9ba82a848a48",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used to acknowledge thanks; ritual reply to “thank you”."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "528a1df4-10e1-43aa-95ce-708cf209e80c",
                                                "sense_id": "f57d90a9-fed9-3934-a9d9-66f55bf6221a",
                                                "text": "Thank you! — Of course!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ad3185eb-0d6c-415c-97dc-1af7d5e069ec",
                        "source_entry_id": "7f8b5f7d-b5de-3442-8c52-ecda8e541bad",
                        "source_sense_id": "f771e171-3c03-35b8-9555-d97faa227226",
                        "target_lang_word": "why",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "why",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6d201baf-9ad1-31a6-a66f-d73027061a13",
                                        "entry_id": "ec999d8a-a48e-3fa6-95e3-7f88f4a908f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "For what cause, reason, or purpose.",
                                            "Introducing a complete question."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "interrogative",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48ae931c-66ca-47c0-87df-c1f307f9f46a",
                                                "sense_id": "6d201baf-9ad1-31a6-a66f-d73027061a13",
                                                "text": "Why is the sky blue?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e4c415c-8972-4b3f-b529-f924be52127f",
                                                "sense_id": "6d201baf-9ad1-31a6-a66f-d73027061a13",
                                                "text": "Why did you do that?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78197ef8-3640-47c2-b668-64e0874ccd91",
                                                "sense_id": "6d201baf-9ad1-31a6-a66f-d73027061a13",
                                                "text": "I don’t know why he did that"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34ce33fe-deb7-47f0-93e2-16d0ffca03a8",
                                                "sense_id": "6d201baf-9ad1-31a6-a66f-d73027061a13",
                                                "text": "Tell me why the moon changes phase."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef5fe2c9-7391-40b7-ba0e-69aeec4c0c12",
                                                "sense_id": "6d201baf-9ad1-31a6-a66f-d73027061a13",
                                                "text": "Why do you have a map of the world?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ddf87375-7759-31ed-8976-dccc03b09895",
                                        "entry_id": "ec999d8a-a48e-3fa6-95e3-7f88f4a908f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "For what cause, reason, or purpose.",
                                            "Introducing a complete question.",
                                            "With a negative, used rhetorically to make a suggestion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "interrogative",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa3cf6a7-c2dd-48e6-b0cd-1b214e5036ee",
                                                "sense_id": "ddf87375-7759-31ed-8976-dccc03b09895",
                                                "text": "Why don't you ask her out for dinner?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c08a33e3-ceb0-39ba-9ff7-a85aedf3941e",
                                        "entry_id": "ec999d8a-a48e-3fa6-95e3-7f88f4a908f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "For what cause, reason, or purpose.",
                                            "Introducing a verb phrase (bare infinitive clause)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "interrogative",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "daee35ba-23f0-4db7-89af-01b96d624890",
                                                "sense_id": "c08a33e3-ceb0-39ba-9ff7-a85aedf3941e",
                                                "text": "Why spend money on something you already get for free?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e7908c2-ed07-4cfa-997b-c349e9cdebf1",
                                                "sense_id": "c08a33e3-ceb0-39ba-9ff7-a85aedf3941e",
                                                "text": "Why not tell him how you feel?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fec05316-34e4-3af4-b04b-5e66f5e33d42",
                                        "entry_id": "ec999d8a-a48e-3fa6-95e3-7f88f4a908f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "For what cause, reason, or purpose.",
                                            "Introducing a noun or other phrase."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "interrogative",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61c330b3-d0f1-44f1-a4cd-4ffac597b1b7",
                                                "sense_id": "fec05316-34e4-3af4-b04b-5e66f5e33d42",
                                                "text": "Why him? Why not someone taller?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c462fb71-7776-39a9-8091-cade356b4d32",
                                        "entry_id": "ec999d8a-a48e-3fa6-95e3-7f88f4a908f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "For which cause, reason, or purpose."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "relative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fca3cdf5-f8c8-4c33-b036-a32fb0b21077",
                                                "sense_id": "c462fb71-7776-39a9-8091-cade356b4d32",
                                                "text": "That's the reason why I did that."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a8ef221-ac01-317f-8455-29760793412d",
                                        "entry_id": "ec999d8a-a48e-3fa6-95e3-7f88f4a908f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The cause, reason, or purpose for which."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77f8b5d4-f910-4a71-87c7-74dd39ed1eb5",
                                                "sense_id": "1a8ef221-ac01-317f-8455-29760793412d",
                                                "text": "That is why the sky is blue."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe8c410e-5e6e-4617-9561-7d0f12371e0e",
                                                "sense_id": "1a8ef221-ac01-317f-8455-29760793412d",
                                                "text": "Plastics are energy-rich substances, which is why many of them burn so readily. Any organism that could unlock and use that energy would do well in the Anthropocene. Terrestrial bacteria and fungi which can manage this trick are already familiar to experts in the field."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "why",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "660916ea-3a9a-38d3-ad80-7448f7e927a2",
                                        "entry_id": "f8445bc0-84ed-3926-a5c1-3cc36402a6a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Reason."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "057243d5-1ad4-41fc-b67f-21b3f58347af",
                                                "sense_id": "660916ea-3a9a-38d3-ad80-7448f7e927a2",
                                                "text": "A good article will cover the who, the what, the when, the where, the why and the how."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b81a0814-ee5f-48d1-a8c2-4039289082d4",
                                                "sense_id": "660916ea-3a9a-38d3-ad80-7448f7e927a2",
                                                "text": "Within months of leaving, she became the new owner of Dream Body Recovery in Miami, which has three rooms that can accommodate up to six clients. “Being a part of this journey with other ladies, knowing how it changed my life, that’s my why,” she told me."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "why",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c09b9c77-fd8c-360e-ab5a-e7915299607f",
                                        "entry_id": "72628d4a-273f-3d1f-9b64-b4e0e503d001",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An exclamation used to express pleasant or unpleasant mild surprise, indignation, or impatience."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b670d98-da79-41ba-9b89-ca1062685461",
                                                "sense_id": "c09b9c77-fd8c-360e-ab5a-e7915299607f",
                                                "text": "Why, that’s ridiculous!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a5fe01c-cbec-43f4-8b09-58e454ca08e2",
                                                "sense_id": "c09b9c77-fd8c-360e-ab5a-e7915299607f",
                                                "text": "Why, how kind of you!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce2d2481-8d90-4b8a-a811-7fea1aad591e",
                                                "sense_id": "c09b9c77-fd8c-360e-ab5a-e7915299607f",
                                                "text": "Why yes, that’s true."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0317fb8b-bbe0-43a8-b75a-6f7787f9adfd",
                                                "sense_id": "c09b9c77-fd8c-360e-ab5a-e7915299607f",
